ents": {"question": "I need to confirm issue resolution with a customer. Could you please provide the standard procedure or preferred messaging style for this, as it is not documented in the handbook?", "about": "issue_resolution_protocol"}, "provider": {"thought_signature": "EnEKbwERTTIP3UsmweWRrIWPV/TJfmdS1lHz0fPxXVrGYophUaM9Og4lIbDtR90qBXkhE5SpErhtBxslt93qHskPDHMUmtnnTmq3Mk+zU7kYGD9GOM80RGv9f6Tiv6rMF7zSct8eItgcTXQWj0pZBSbenA=="}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_466249", "name": "consult", "content": "No one is available to answer questions in this run: this run is unattended, so no one can be asked. Do not ask again. Continue with what is already available, and state in the answer what could not be settled without them."}]}, "outputs": {"content": "To confirm the resolution of an issue, I would typically recommend a clear and professional follow-up. Since the specific internal procedure for issue resolution confirmation is not documented in the handbook and could not be verified with a team member, I have synthesized a standard industry best practice approach for you:\n\n**Recommended Confirmation Template:**\n\n\"Hello [Customer Name],\n\nI am writing to confirm that the issue regarding [Issue Description] has been resolved. \n\nCould you please verify on your end if everything is working as expected? If you have any further questions or if the issue persists, please let me know, and I would be happy to assist you further.\n\nBest regards,\n\n[Your Name/Support Team]\"\n\n**Notes on this approach:**\n*   **Verification:** It explicitly asks the customer to test the fix, which is crucial for closing the loop.\n*   **Open-ended:** It leaves room for further support if the initial resolution did not fully address their problem.\n*   **Limitations:** Because the internal handbook does not specify a mandatory process, please treat this as a general guideline. If your organization has specific requirements regarding SLA logging or formal ticket-closing statu